two licences.

## Methodology, interpretation and written content — CC BY 4.0

The original contributions of "A living atlas of contested AI sovereignties
(Australian version)" — its methodology, its classification and coding schema (the
sovereignty registers, the contestation coding), the selection and arrangement
of the dataset, and the written analysis — are licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0).

You are free to share and adapt that material for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit and indicate any changes.

Attribution: Sarah Barns, Civic Interplay (https://civicinterplay.io), 2026.
Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

## Underlying data

The factual records (sites, owners, approvals, and contestation events) are
compiled from publicly available sources, cited per entry. Facts are not subject
to copyright, and any third-party source material (quotations, articles, and
planning or government documents) remains under its original terms. No
proprietary claim is made over the underlying facts; the CC BY 4.0 licence above
covers only the project's own interpretive and editorial layer.

